      "description": "Nexus® is an extensive family of three 'connected' typefaces, partly based on Majoor's Seria, but conceived much more as a workhorse typeface. The starting point was Nexus Serif. From this, a sans serif version was derived: Nexus Sans. A third member then followed, a slab-serif-like design called Nexus Mix, in turn derived from the sans.\n\nNexus Serif Italic comes with two series of elegant swash capitals, with lowercase swashes available in both long and short end-swash versions. It also includes a range of special characters, such as squares, circles, stars, and arrows, in both solid and outline versions.",
